Architecture Description:
Step 1: Local Training on First Dataset
Client 1 trains its local model on Set 1 and sends the resulting model weights to the Server.

Client 2 does the same—trains on Set 1 and sends its weights to the Server.

Step 2: Aggregation
The Server aggregates the weights from both clients (commonly by averaging them).

Step 3: Model Distribution
The Server sends the aggregated model back to both clients.

Step 4: Local Training on Second Dataset
Client 1 trains the received aggregated model on Set 2 and sends the updated weights to the Server.

Client 2 trains on Set 2 and sends its updated weights to the Server.

Step 5: Final Aggregation
The Server aggregates the updated weights from both clients into the final model.

Step 6: Final Model Distribution
The Server sends the final model to both clients.
